-- #1281 — THE SAME-INDEX, DIFFERENT-FIELD-TYPE spelling of the cross-module record
-- identity defect.  Kept as a live cell because its `must_fail` pin
-- (`1281-xmod-record-differing-field-type-native-segfault/`) DRAINED when #1382 was
-- fixed and was deleted with it; without this the shape would lose its coverage.
--
-- It is a genuinely different cell from `record_xmod_field_type_swap/`: there the
-- two records disagree about field ORDER, here they agree about order and disagree
-- about the field's TYPE, so what the wrong record buys is the wrong SLOT
-- REPRESENTATION (an unboxed Float cell read as a tagged Int) rather than the wrong
-- offset.
--
-- This module imports `aaf` — NOT `Cfg` — from `aacfg`, and `Cfg` only from `zzcfg`.
-- `Cfg` at the literal below can therefore only mean zzcfg's, the sole `Cfg` this
-- module ever brings into scope.
--
-- Expected output, derived BY HAND before anything was run: `Cfg { fld = 7 }` then
-- `.fld`, so `7`.
--
-- Counterfactual, measured on THIS directory rather than reasoned: with
-- `compiler/types/typecheck.mdk` restored to `c5fda728` and nothing else changed,
-- `medaka build` on this entry exits 0 and the produced binary exits 139 with
-- `runtime error [E-FATAL-SIGNAL]: fatal memory fault (segmentation fault)` before
-- printing anything.  (That `medaka run` stayed correct is the deleted
-- `must_fail_fixtures/1281-…` row's recorded observation, not one re-run here.)
import aacfg.{aaf}
import zzcfg.{Cfg}

v : Cfg
v = Cfg { fld = 7 }

-- ⚠️ `putStrLn (intToString …)`, not `println`: this corpus's emit driver
-- (`test/bin/llvm_emit_modules_main`, via `diff_compiler_llvm_modules.sh`) reports
-- `unbound variable 'println'` — measured — where `medaka build` on the same file
-- is fine.  The deleted `must_fail_fixtures/1281-…/main.mdk` used `println` because
-- it ran under `build-run`, which does not have that restriction.
main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (intToString v.fld)
